// §249 — PERSIAN. Keyed by the English source (normalized innerHTML for rich
// blocks, text for plate labels); see src/explain-i18n.js for why.
//
// Vocabulary is the SAME register tier one's chrome uses (src/i18n.js), and it
// is Persian's own, not Arabic's: Persian horology borrows from French, so the
// trade's loanwords stand where they are the trade's words — انکر for the
// pallet fork, بالانس for the balance, پینیون for a pinion, فوزه for the fusee
// — beside Persian ones: گریز اهرمی سوئیسی, چرخ گریز, فنر مویی, فنر اصلی,
// بشکه, زنجیر, تاج, چرخ ستونی. One movement cannot have two names for a part.
//
// The second right-to-left table, and like Arabic's the strings do not know
// it: the mirroring is the document's (LOCALES' `dir`), the plates keep
// direction: ltr, and the back links' arrows are mirrored by hand. Orthography
// is Persian's: ی and ک, never Arabic ي and ك; the zero-width non-joiner
// inside a word (می‌شود، چرخ‌دنده‌ها); no ezafe hamza, whose combining mark
// would stop the glossary linker matching the word it sits on.
//
// NUMBERS AND <code> ARE NOT TRANSLATED, and they are WESTERN DIGITS — a ۱ is
// not a number to tools/explain-i18n.mjs. Emphasis the English carries as
// CAPITALS rides the wording, never an added tag. "مدل‌سازی‌شده" vs
// "شبیه‌سازی‌شده" tracks the repo's modelled/simulated distinction exactly;
// HONESTY.fa gates it, and the bare noun مدل is deliberately not the honesty word.
